{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1785364622951,"sessionID":"ses_04ff9ee89ffe21MRExDwpvIhCN","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"bash","callID":"2KhNZhJWjBYNrgVQIdYIcQh68WTuy0ZG","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"sh /workspace/.agent_scripts/search.sh \"Neural Networks fundamentals backpropagation gradient descent\""},"output":"1. A Data Scientist’s Guide to Gradient Descent and Backpropagation Algorithms | NVIDIA Technical Blog\nhttps://developer.nvidia.com/blog/a-data-scientists-guide-to-gradient-descent-and-backpropagation-algorithms/\nArtificial Neural Networks (ANNs) are the basis of machine learning models and simulate human brain learning to accomplish human-like performance in machines. Gradient Descent is an optimization algorithm used to minimize the cost function by adjusting the weights and biases in a neural network, guiding the search for optimal parameter values. Backpropagation is the mechanism that iteratively ...\n\n2. Backpropagation - Wikipedia\nhttps://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Backpropagation\nThis includes changing model parameters ... gradient descent, or as an intermediate step in a more complicated optimizer, such as Adaptive Moment Estimation. Backpropagation had multiple discoveries and partial discoveries, with a tangled history and terminology (see § History). Some other names for the technique include \"reverse mode of automatic differentiation\" or \"reverse accumulation\". Backpropagation computes the gradient in weight space of a feedforward neural network, with respect ...\n\n3. machine learning - How does Gradient Descent and Backpropagation work together? - Data Science Stack Exchange\nhttps://datascience.stackexchange.com/questions/44703/how-does-gradient-descent-and-backpropagation-work-together\nPlease forgive me as I am new to this. I have attached a diagram trying to model my understanding of neural network and Back-propagation? From videos on Coursera and resources online I formed the More on datascience.stackexchange.com\n\n4. How Does Gradient Descent and Backpropagation Work Together?\nhttps://www.geeksforgeeks.org/machine-learning/how-does-gradient-descent-and-backpropagation-work-together/\nTogether, gradient descent and backpropagation form the backbone of training neural networks, allowing models to learn from data and improve their performance over time. Conclusion: Gradient descent and backpropagation work together synergistically to train neural networks by iteratively updating the model parameters to minimize the loss function.\n\n5. Neural networks and deep learning\nhttp://neuralnetworksanddeeplearning.com/chap2.html\nAs I've described it above, the backpropagation algorithm computes the gradient of the cost function for a single training example, $C = C_x$. In practice, it's common to combine backpropagation with a learning algorithm such as stochastic gradient descent, in which we compute the gradient ...\n\n6. Backpropagation: Step-By-Step Derivation - Towards Data Science\nhttps://towardsdatascience.com/backpropagation-step-by-step-derivation-99ac8fbdcc28/\nWe use small batches of random training samples (normally between 10 to 1,000 examples) for the gradient updates. This reduces the noise in SGD but is still more efficient than full-batch updates, and it is the most common form to train neural networks. Backpropagation: The Complete Algorithm\n\n7. Backpropagation & Gradient Descent Explained: With Derivation and Code\nhttps://www.quarkml.com/2023/02/backpropagation-and-gradient-descent-simplified.html\nIn this article, we'll explore in-depth how Backpropagation works with Gradient Descent to train Neural Networks.\n\n8. Gradient Descent Fundamentals | CodeSignal Learn\nhttps://codesignal.com/learn/courses/training-neural-networks-the-backpropagation-algorithm-1/lessons/gradient-descent-fundamentals\nWhile our 1D example directly computed ... complexity, gradient descent follows the same fundamental principle: iteratively update parameters by moving in the direction that reduces the loss function most rapidly....\n\n9. How Neural Networks Learn: Gradient Descent, Backpropagation, and ...\nhttps://medium.com/@theshubhamgoel/how-neural-networks-learn-gradient-descent-backpropagation-and-building-intuition-32d807542e31\nChollet covers derivatives, gradients, stochastic gradient descent, and backpropagation — the engine that makes neural networks actually work.\n\n10. Understanding Backpropagation and Gradient Descent in Neural Networks - DEV Community\nhttps://dev.to/patilmanas/understanding-backpropagation-and-gradient-descent-in-neural-networks-2heb\nWithout these, neural networks would just be complex calculators spitting out random values. Thanks to backpropagation, networks can learn from their mistakes, and thanks to gradient descent, they can improve continuously.\n\n","metadata":{"output":"1. A Data Scientist’s Guide to Gradient Descent and Backpropagation Algorithms | NVIDIA Technical Blog\nhttps://developer.nvidia.com/blog/a-data-scientists-guide-to-gradient-descent-and-backpropagation-algorithms/\nArtificial Neural Networks (ANNs) are the basis of machine learning models and simulate human brain learning to accomplish human-like performance in machines. Gradient Descent is an optimization algorithm used to minimize the cost function by adjusting the weights and biases in a neural network, guiding the search for optimal parameter values. Backpropagation is the mechanism that iteratively ...\n\n2. Backpropagation - Wikipedia\nhttps://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Backpropagation\nThis includes changing model parameters ... gradient descent, or as an intermediate step in a more complicated optimizer, such as Adaptive Moment Estimation. Backpropagation had multiple discoveries and partial discoveries, with a tangled history and terminology (see § History). Some other names for the technique include \"reverse mode of automatic differentiation\" or \"reverse accumulation\". Backpropagation computes the gradient in weight space o